###Ingredients
Large chunk of pumpkin chopped into even, bite sized pieces  
2 tbsp soy sauce  
2 tbsp olive oil  
large knob of butter  
large clove of smooshed garlic  
¼ finely diced red onion  
½ leek diced into lentil sized pieces  
Large bunch of silverbeet or spinach  
2 large field mushrooms  
1 tin, or equivalent cooked puy or brown lentils  
Salt to taste  
1 tsp ground black pepper  


###Method

1. Set the oven to 180ºc fan or 190ºc normal oven
2. Place large oven proof low sided pan on medium to high heat
3. Put large pot of salted water 
4. Set aside large bowl of cold (iced) water
5. Chop pumpkin into bite sized pieces.  Place in large bowl and coat with black pepper, soy sauce and olive oil
6. Tip pumpkin and residual olive oil and soy into hot pan and brown the pieces on all sides
7. Once browned, bake in oven until cooked but still slightly firm
8. Place large, heavy based pan on medium heat
9. Finely chop onion, leek and mushrooms to equal sizes, roughly the size of the lentils
10. Smoosh the garlic clove
11. Add butter and oil to pan.  When the butter is melted and a bit bubbly, add the onions, mushrooms, leek and garlic
12. Add salt and lots of black pepper and cook through until soft and beginning to caramelise
13. Remove pumpkin from oven and set aside
14. Add draned and rinsed lentils to mushroom mix and stir through
15. Blanch the silverbeet for 2 minutes.  Drain and plunge into cold water to stop cooking
16. Drain and squeeze out extra water from silverbeet
17. Roughly chop silverbeet and add to lentil mix
18. Turn off the lentil pan and add the pumpkin
19. Serve warm with fresh chopped parsley and lemon zest
